@(12 = 12-20) Distress has been caused in your city @wSN{Larsam}, which you have chosen in your heart. The broad squares where days have been passed in merriment  @varh[t3205.v3]{have been reduced to } @vart[t3205.v4,t3205.v3]{@varn{1 ms. has instead:} are left (?) in } silence. Your commendable troops who were assembled have been annihilated (?) like reeds from a reed fence splitting apart. Your young men have been harvested like barley at the due time; they have been picked and have been plucked like ripened fruit (?). The people have been smashed like terracotta figurines; they (?) have perished all together. An evil storm took away the little ones from the laps (?) of their mothers. The people ……; their appearance has been (?) changed. Overwhelming troops have been set loose, …… the Land …… like flour. O youthful @wDN{Utu}, like an enemy you stand aside from your city @wSN{Larsam}.

#etcsl#altGrpo
#etcsl#alt t3205.v3 t3205.v4
#etcsl#altGrpc

@(21 = 21-29) The mountain land of @wGN{Elam} where there are no dead in great numbers (?) like ……, and @wGN{Subir}, a heavy cloud, which knows no reverence even towards the gods -- these districts have not been weakened; their time has not yet come.  @varh[t3205.v5]{The @wEN{Šimaškian} does not elect @fsux{nugig} or @fsux{lukur} priestesses for the places of the gods } @vart[t3205.v6,t3205.v5]{@varn{1 ms. has instead:} The @wEN{Šimaškian} knows neither his god nor those elected @fsux{nugig} and @fsux{lukur} priestesses } @vart[t3205.v7,t3205.v5]{@varn{1 other ms. has instead:} The @wEN{Šimaškian} …… neither the @fsux{nugig} nor the @fsux{nubar} priestesses for the places of the gods }. His soldiers are numerous like grass; his seed  @varh[t3205.v8]{is widespread } @vart[t3205.v9,t3205.v8]{@varn{1 ms. has instead:} is indeed exalted }. He who lives in tents, who does not know of the places of the gods: like a wild beast which mounts, he knows nothing of  @varh[t3205.v10]{@fsux{eša} flour nor prayers } @vart[t3205.v11,t3205.v10]{@varn{1 ms. has instead:} flour and the offering of prayers }. The evil @fsux{namtar} demon and the distressing @fsux{asag} demon  @varh[t3205.v12]{have not carried him off (?) } @vart[t3205.v13,t3205.v12]{@varn{1 ms. has instead:} do not approach him }. Who …… a divine oath is committing sacrilege, yet his troops are in good health.

